      "description": "Released to the public as part of the Department of Energy's Open Energy Data Initiative, the [National Solar Radiation Database (NSRDB)](https://nsrdb.nrel.gov/) is a serially complete collection of hourly and half-hourly values of the three most common measurements of solar radiation – global horizontal, direct normal, and diffuse horizontal irradiance — and meteorological data. These data have been collected at a sufficient number of locations and temporal and spatial scales to accurately represent regional solar radiation climates.",
